Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 21:16:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Property-based tests: VirtualiZarr kerchunk manifests vs.
 the data they describe

Hypothesis generates random datasets (1-3 dims, up to 6 per dim, nine
numeric dtypes, NaN masking with and without an explicit _FillValue,
contiguous or chunked HDF5 layout with any subset of shuffle/deflate/
fletcher32, int or float coordinates), writes them as NetCDF4, indexes the
file with VirtualiZarr's HDFParser, and asserts read_zarr(manifest,
format='kerchunk') equals the dataset and equals the same data read from a
real Zarr v2 store. A second property checks read_zarr_metadata against the
.zarray documents in the manifest.

make test_kerchunk runs the default profile, make test_kerchunk_deep the
long search; HYPOTHESIS_PROFILE selects ci/default/deep.
